Subject: [PATCH] elf: accept the optional missing-file errno in rtld diagnostics

These tests cover missing executable handling and the -- delimiter.
With /etc/ld.so.cache absent,
tunable cache initialization can add ENOENT even with --inhibit-cache.
The same packaged loader emits no suffix when a valid cache is present.

Accept only the literal ENOENT suffix; retain the exact executable name,
fatal message, exit status 127 and single-line checks. This also covers
the diagnostic variation reported in upstream BZ 34361:
https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=34361

--- a/elf/tst-rtld-dash-dash.sh
+++ b/elf/tst-rtld-dash-dash.sh
@@ -19,8 +19,8 @@
 
 export LC_ALL=C
 
-# --inhibit-cache to suppress "No such file or directory" message when
-# /etc/ld.so.cache does not exist.
+# Cache initialization can add ENOENT even with --inhibit-cache. Accept
+# only that suffix; keep the executable, delimiter and status checks.
 rtld="$1 --inhibit-cache"
 tmp_out="$(mktemp)"
 
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 cat "$tmp_out"
 
 if test $status -eq 127 \
-	&& grep -q "^--program-does-not-exist: error while loading shared libraries: --program-does-not-exist: cannot open shared object file$" "$tmp_out" \
+	&& grep -Eq "^--program-does-not-exist: error while loading shared libraries: --program-does-not-exist: cannot open shared object file(: No such file or directory)?$" "$tmp_out" \
 	&& test "$(wc -l < "$tmp_out")" -eq 1 ; then
     status=0
 else
--- a/elf/tst-rtld-does-not-exist.sh
+++ b/elf/tst-rtld-does-not-exist.sh
@@ -19,8 +19,8 @@
 
